+### 3.10 Item Portraits → one image per item
+
+Figma: section `40:150`. Six samples (`40:120` to `40:125`: Torch, Ladder, Door, Fence, Chest, Bed),
+each a 128 x 128 rectangle with an image fill and corner radius 12. Designer note: *"120 item
+portraits in total, and more are added every update. The item detail pane shows one at a time at
+128 x 128."*
+
+- **No sprite sheet.** Only one is shown at a time, so a sheet would mean downloading 15 or more
+  portraits to show one. The set also grows every update, which would mean redoing the sheets each
+  time. Each portrait is its own asset.
+- Export each at 2x → **256 x 256**, with the **corner radius set to 0** (square). The rounding
+  comes from a `UICorner` in Roblox, so it stays consistent and easy to change.
+- If a portrait's source image is smaller than 256 x 256, export it anyway at 256 but tell the
+  designer. It will look soft on 4K.
+- Name files after the item, e.g. `ItemPortrait_Torch.png`, so they line up with item ids.
+
+ImageLabel (on top of the defaults):
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Image` | that item's asset id |
+| `Size` | `UDim2.fromOffset(128, 128)` |
+| child `UICorner` | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 12)` |
+
