+## 4. Built from Roblox UI objects (nothing to export)
+
+All of these are solid fills, simple strokes, rounded corners, and text, which Roblox draws
+natively. Building them keeps text localizable and easy to change. Text uses the **Builder Sans**
+font family in Roblox (`Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/BuilderSans.json", <weight>)`).
+
+### 4.1 Prompts / Keyboard
+
+Figma: section `40:129`. Ten keys (B, I, E, Q, 1, 2, 3 at 40 x 40; Esc, Tab, Shift at 56 x 40). Each
+has corner radius 6, light fill, a 2 px grey **inside** stroke, and a Bold 18 px label. Designer note:
+*"Key prompts shown next to actions on PC."*
+
+Build one key component that takes the label text, so any key can be shown without new art:
+
+- `Frame`: `Size` 40 x 40 (56 x 40 for Esc / Tab / Shift), `BackgroundColor3 = Color3.fromRGB(235, 237, 242)`
+- `UICorner`: `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 6)`
+- `UIStroke`: `Thickness = 2`, `Color = Color3.fromRGB(153, 157, 171)`, `ApplyStrokeMode = Border`,
+  `BorderStrokePosition = Inner` to match Figma's inside stroke. On a Studio build without that
+  property, the stroke draws outside, so make the Frame 36 x 36 (52 x 36) to keep the same outer size.
+- `TextLabel`: fills the frame, `BackgroundTransparency = 1`, Builder Sans **Bold**, `TextSize = 18`,
+  `TextColor3 = Color3.fromRGB(31, 33, 41)`, centred both ways.
+
+### 4.2 Card / Ribbon
+
+Figma: frame `40:141`, 240 x 56, red fill. Only the **top-left and bottom-right** corners are rounded
+(radius 16, `rectangleCornerRadii [16, 0, 16, 0]`). Label "NEW", Builder Sans ExtraBold 22, white.
+
+`UICorner` rounds all four corners, so:
+
+- `Frame` 240 x 56, `BackgroundColor3 = Color3.fromRGB(222, 67, 82)`, `UICorner` radius 16.
+- Two 16 x 16 `Frame`s, same colour, no corner, placed in the **top-right** and **bottom-left**
+  corners to square them off.
+- `TextLabel` "NEW" centred: Builder Sans **ExtraBold**, `TextSize = 22`, white. It must stay real
+  text for localization.
+
+### 4.3 Profile Card
+
+Figma: frame `40:153`, 360 x 190, radius 16, fill `Color3.fromRGB(33, 37, 54)`.
+
+- `Frame` + `UICorner` radius 16.
+- **Avatar** (`40:151`, 150 x 150 circle): designer note *"placeholder photo, use the player's
+  headshot."* **Do not export the placeholder.** Use an `ImageLabel` 150 x 150 at offset (20, 20)
+  with `Image = "rbxthumb://type=AvatarHeadShot&id=<userId>&w=352&h=352"`. 352 is the smallest
+  headshot size that's still sharp at 2x. Add a `UICorner` with `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0.5, 0)` to
+  make it round.
+
+### 4.4 Glass Card
+
+Figma: frame `40:155`, 320 x 200, radius 16, white fill at 10%, 1 px white stroke at 20%,
+**background blur 20**. Title "Inventory", Builder Sans Bold 22, white.
+
+- `Frame`: `BackgroundColor3` white, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.9`, `UICorner` radius 16.
+- `UIStroke`: `Thickness = 1`, white, `Transparency = 0.8`.
+- `TextLabel` title at (24, 20): Builder Sans **Bold**, `TextSize = 22`, white.
+- **Background blur can't be done.** Roblox has no per-element blur for 2D UI (`BlurEffect` blurs
+  the whole 3D view), and it can't be exported either, because it depends on what's behind the card.
+  Tell the designer it will ship without the blur. If the card is hard to read over busy scenes,
+  raise the fill opacity (e.g. `BackgroundTransparency = 0.8`) or darken it.
+
+### 4.5 Progress Bar
+
+Figma: frame `40:158`, 300 x 12, radius 6, white at 12%, with a green `Fill` (`40:156`). Designer
+note: *"Fill width follows quest progress."*
+
+- Track `Frame`: 300 x 12, white, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.88`, `UICorner` radius 6.
+- Fill `Frame`: `Size = UDim2.fromScale(progress, 1)`,
+  `BackgroundColor3 = Color3.fromRGB(87, 209, 118)`, `UICorner` radius 6.
+- Below 12 px of fill the rounded ends get squashed. Either hide the fill at 0, or set
+  `ClipsDescendants` on the track and give the fill a minimum width of 12.
